# Real scientific functions with checked finite domains, in radians for sin/cos.
let values be a list of 0, 1, 2.
let exponentials be map every x in values to (exp of x).
let logarithms be map every x in (a list of 1, 2, 4) to (ln of x).
assert exp of 0 is equal to 1.0.
assert ln of 1 is equal to 0.0.
assert sin of 0 is equal to 0.0.
assert cos of 0 is equal to 1.0.
assert length of exponentials is equal to 3.
assert length of logarithms is equal to 3.
print "scientific math OK".
